>In article <1993Feb2.221702.10893@midway.uchicago.edu> wen5@midway.uchicago.edu writes:
>
>I have had a problem with some monsters, like minotaurs, as pets in NetHack
>3.0.  Mainly, what do you feed them?

If it's a lack of reality you're referring to, well, this is Nethack.  As
for feeding Minotaurs, they eat anything your dog eats.  In 3.1, however,
poison resistant pets WILL EAT POISONOUS CORPSES.

>  Therefore, my personal favorites have
>been dragons.  Vicious devils, those, but they can cause problems like killing
>priests in temples when you really wanted to bump up your AC with an offering.

Dragons suck.  They can't do enough damage quickly enough to avoid being
killed by more powerful monsters, and they don't regenerate.  Olog-hai's
will regenerate so rapidly that they can kill three or four shopkeepers
and be ready for some ochre jellies.  It is of course speeded and invisible.

>Also, don't forget you can speed up these pets and make them invisible with
>the right wands.  A dragon can kill a shopkeeper in a real hurry, and they
>eat almost any corpse.

I have an Olog-hai now who kills shopkeepers in one round.  Boom.  Shopkeeper
jerky all over the screen.  I think dragons would be better pets if they
used their breath weapons.  Otherwise, I think their hard pets to keep alive
on lower levels.  Minotaurs don't regenerate either, but they can do much
more damage than Olog-hai's.
>
Well, one problem with my polymorph pet spoiler is this:

If you polymorph your pet into something sessile (brown mold or blue jelly),
it will not move, and will therefore be unpolymorphable.

